==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Holy Dragon Megidora''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Megidora''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Megidora is a very good unit against Floating enemies. He can outrange many of them, and counter them with his slow/knockback effects, preventing them from advancing, a valuable aspect considering these enemies consist of many nasty, short-ranged pushers. He is also a moderate generalist thanks to his stats. However, you should protect him properly as he has a tendency to recklessly rush into frontlines due to high movement speed.

However, just like any unit with knockback, he must be used with care if Floating enemies are supported by foes of other traits, as he might knock them away and put your remaining units into the range of other threats. Unfortunately, this is the very reason he is outclassed. A great variety of accessible anti-floating options exist in the form of [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]], who all usually do not share the issue, and their low range reduces the risks of exposure of other units to other threats.

==='''True Form'''===
God-Emperor Megidora gains higher health, attack power, attack range and movement speed. Though these boosts make him a better generalist, the movement speed increase means that Megidora will sometimes rush into enemy frontlines and die quicker. To make matters worse, his knockback count is not increased, meaning that boost in particular may be pointless.

==='''Talents'''===
It is not recommended to unlock Megidora's talents as they are extremely expensive, and don't resolve most of his issues.

The stat talents are not very important, as Megidora is typically outclassed by other units such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] (440 range), and they don't offer much for what he does. '''Wave Attacks''' do allow him to have a bigger impact due to his relatively fast attack rate and high damage, but the chances are too low for any meaningful answers.

'''Knockback''' and '''Curse Immunity''' are all the better options, as Megidora is vulnerable to curse and his attacks do not have guaranteed effects. Unfortunately, as useful as they can be, Megidora does not stand well to Relics and could only be situationally used when [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] is the main threat. Boosting his knockback allows him to hinder pushers better, but that's how far it goes, since the aforementioned anti-Floating units actually do better without knockback due to their low range, and they can eliminate many Floating enemies anyway.

While his Ultra Talents don't expand Megidora much, he sees slightly better matchups. '''Target Metal''' is straight-up useless for the same reason he is outclassed against Floating enemies, but '''Target Relic''' is a decent one if his Curse Immunity talent has been purchased, as he can potentially delay many Relics that he outranges. '''Cost Down''', while good to have due to his high cost, isn't necessary with the extreme cooldown time he has.

